the target language is: prolog.

% Spike: the LE twin of rules.l4, written by hand the way the translator of
% the design notes l4.md would write it. The expected answers are the
% L4 evaluator's (node l4run.mjs rules.l4). LE prints a list without commas.

the templates are:
    the name of *a person* is *a text*; undefined.
    the age of *a person* is *a number*; undefined.
    the citizenship of *a person* is *a text*; undefined.
    the annual income of *a person* is *an amount*; undefined.
    *a person* has a criminal record; undefined.
    *an applicant* is eligible for benefit.
    *an applicant* is a qualifying resident.
    *an applicant* is of age.
    *an applicant* meets the income threshold.
    *an applicant* is disqualified.
    the income tax owed on *an income* is *an amount*.
    the amount of *an income* in the first bracket is *an amount*.
    the amount of *an income* in the second bracket is *an amount*.
    all of *a list* are positive.

the knowledge base benefit includes:

an applicant is eligible for benefit if
    the applicant is a qualifying resident
    and the applicant is of age
    and the applicant meets the income threshold
    and it is not the case that
        the applicant is disqualified.

an applicant is a qualifying resident if
    the citizenship of the applicant is "citizen".

an applicant is of age if
    the age of the applicant is an age
    and the age >= 21
    and the age < 65.

an applicant meets the income threshold if
    the annual income of the applicant is an amount
    and the amount < 30000.

an applicant is disqualified if
    the applicant has a criminal record.

the income tax owed on an income is an amount if
    the amount of the income in the first bracket is a first amount
    and the amount of the income in the second bracket is a second amount
    and the amount = the first amount * 0.10 + the second amount * 0.20.

the amount of an income in the first bracket is an amount if
    the income =< 10000 and the amount = the income
    otherwise the amount = 10000.

the amount of an income in the second bracket is an amount if
    the income =< 10000 and the amount = 0
    otherwise the amount = the income - 10000.

all of a list are positive if
    for all cases in which
        a number is in the list
    it is the case that
        the number > 0.

scenario people is:
    the name of ann is "ann".
    the age of ann is 30.
    the citizenship of ann is "citizen".
    the annual income of ann is 20000.
    the name of bob is "bob".
    the age of bob is 30.
    the citizenship of bob is "citizen".
    the annual income of bob is 20000.
    bob has a criminal record.
    eligible expects answers ["ann is eligible for benefit"].
    tax1 expects answers ["the income tax owed on 8000 is 800.0"].
    tax2 expects answers ["the income tax owed on 25000 is 4000.0"].
    pos1 expects answers ["all of [1 2 3] are positive"].
    pos2 expects answers [].

query eligible is:
    which applicant is eligible for benefit.

query tax1 is:
    the income tax owed on 8000 is which amount.

query tax2 is:
    the income tax owed on 25000 is which amount.

query pos1 is:
    all of [1, 2, 3] are positive.

query pos2 is:
    all of [1, -2, 3] are positive.
